1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,500
世界，充满尚未解开的可能。
The world is filled with possibilities waiting to be unlocked.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:15,000
算法，把一个想法变成可以执行的步骤。
An algorithm turns an idea into executable steps.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:22,500
看不见的规则，编排看得见的世界。
Invisible rules choreograph the visible world.

4
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:30,000
简单的规则，也能孕育复杂而壮丽的结果。
Simple rules can give rise to intricate, magnificent results.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,500
排序，让散落的信息拥有可比较的次序。
Sorting gives scattered information a comparable order.

6
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:45,000
归并排序，先把问题逐层拆小。
Merge sort first divides the problem into smaller parts.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,500
再合并有序片段，让局部秩序汇成整体。
It merges sorted runs until local order becomes global order.

8
00:00:52,500 --> 00:01:00,000
标准归并排序的时间复杂度为 O(n log n)。
Standard merge sort runs in O(n log n) time.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:07,500
在有序数据中，二分查找每次排除约一半候选。
In sorted data, binary search eliminates about half the candidates.

10
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:15,000
比较中点，让搜索范围不断收缩。
Compare the midpoint. Narrow the search interval.

11
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:22,500
随机访问有序数组时，查找只需 O(log n) 次比较。
In a sorted random-access array, search takes O(log n) comparisons.

12
00:01:22,500 --> 00:01:30,000
图，把道路和连接转化为可计算的关系。
A graph turns roads and connections into computable relationships.

13
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:37,500
边权非负时，Dijkstra 逐步确定最短距离。
With nonnegative edge weights, Dijkstra settles shortest distances.

14
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:45,000
每一条最短路径，都来自比较与更新。
Every shortest path emerges from comparison and relaxation.

15
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:52,500
递归，让问题用更小的同类问题来描述。
Recursion describes a problem through smaller instances of itself.

16
00:01:52,500 --> 00:02:00,000
一次分支，一次重复，尺度中诞生新的风景。
A branch. A repetition. New landscapes emerge across scales.

17
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:07,500
终止条件，让递归最终回到可解的起点。
A base case gives recursion a place to stop and resolve.

18
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:15,000
子问题的答案，沿调用层次逐层返回。
Answers return through the layers of recursive calls.

19
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:22,500
动态规划，把重复的子问题变成可以复用的答案。
Dynamic programming turns repeated subproblems into reusable answers.

20
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:30,000
状态记录过去，转移连接下一步。
States record what is known. Transitions connect what comes next.

21
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:37,500
在合适的状态和转移下，逐步构建整体解。
With suitable states and transitions, build the full solution step by step.

22
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:45,000
存储结果节省重复计算，也带来空间成本。
Storing results avoids repeated work, at the cost of memory.

23
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:52,500
复杂信号，可以分解为不同频率的成分。
A complex signal can be decomposed into frequency components.

24
00:02:52,500 --> 00:03:00,000
FFT 利用结构与对称，加速离散傅里叶变换。
The FFT exploits structure and symmetry to accelerate the DFT.

25
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:07,500
时域中的叠加，在频域中显露层次。
Superposition in time reveals its components in frequency.

26
00:03:07,500 --> 00:03:15,000
常见 FFT 将变换计算降至 O(n log n)。
Common FFT algorithms compute the transform in O(n log n).

27
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:22,500
优化，为每一次选择定义一个目标。
Optimization gives each choice an objective.

28
00:03:22,500 --> 00:03:30,000
梯度下降，沿局部最陡下降方向更新。
Gradient descent updates along the direction of steepest local decrease.

29
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:37,500
非凸问题中，局部最优未必是全局最优。
For nonconvex problems, a local optimum need not be global.

30
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:45,000
步长、初始化与停止条件，共同影响结果。
Step size, initialization, and stopping criteria shape the result.

31
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:52,500
复杂度描述规模增长时，计算成本如何变化。
Complexity describes how computational cost grows with input size.

32
00:03:52,500 --> 00:04:00,000
更快，可能需要更多内存；更省，也可能更慢。
Speed may require more memory. Saving memory may cost time.

33
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:07,500
硬件、数据分布和约束，让理论遇见现实。
Hardware, data distributions, and constraints bring theory into practice.

34
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:15,000
边界情况、正确性与验证，是优雅的根基。
Edge cases, correctness, and validation are the foundation of elegance.

35
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:22,500
排序、搜索、递归、优化，共享思考的语言。
Sorting, search, recursion, and optimization share a language of thought.

36
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:30,000
算法之美，在于用清晰的步骤驾驭复杂。
The beauty of algorithms lies in navigating complexity with clear steps.

37
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:37,500
从一条路径，到万千连接。
From a single path to a universe of connections.

38
00:04:37,500 --> 00:04:45,000
真正的力量，来自理解为什么这样前进。
Real power comes from understanding why each step works.

39
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:52,500
理解算法，让思想拥有改变世界的形状。
Understand algorithms. Give ideas the power to shape the world.

40
00:04:52,500 --> 00:05:00,000
算法之美，始于思考，成于创造。
The beauty of algorithms begins in thought and comes alive in creation.
